<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/a1c-blood-glucose-test> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "A1C blood glucose test" ;
    dmo:gradingSystem "N/A" ;
    dmo:nativeEvidenceGrade "1" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Most people with diabetes" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "a1c-blood-glucose-test" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Monitoring" ;
    dmo:statement "The A1C test shows your average blood glucose level over the last 3 months. This test is done at a health care professional’s office or lab. For most people with diabetes, their goal is an A1C level below 7%.1 Your A1C goal may be different if you have other health problems.2 Ask your health care team how often you should have the test and what your goal should be." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "The A1C test shows your average blood glucose level over the last 3 months. This test is done at a health care professional’s office or lab. For most people with diabetes, their goal is an A1C level below 7%.1 Your A1C goal may be different if you have other health problems.2 Ask your health care team how often you should have the test and what your goal should be." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/niddk-managing-diabetes> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/adjust-goals-for-adults-over-age-65-or-with-other-health-problems> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Adjust goals for adults over age 65 or with other health problems" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Adults over age 65 with long-standing diabetes, or those with other health problems such as heart disease, or frequent hypoglycemia" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "adjust-goals-for-adults-over-age-65-or-with-other-health-problems" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Monitoring" ;
    dmo:statement "Your blood glucose goals may be different if you are an adult over age 65 and have had diabetes for a long time. Your blood glucose goals may also be different if you have other health problems, like heart disease, or if your blood glucose often gets too low." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Your blood glucose goals may be different if you are an adult over age 65 and have had diabetes for a long time. Your blood glucose goals may also be different if you have other health problems, like heart disease, or if your blood glucose often gets too low." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/niddk-managing-diabetes> .

