<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/blood-pressure-goal-below-130-80-mm-hg> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Blood pressure goal below 130/80 mm Hg" ;
    dmo:gradingSystem "N/A" ;
    dmo:nativeEvidenceGrade "2,3" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Some people with diabetes" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "blood-pressure-goal-below-130-80-mm-hg" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Monitoring" ;
    dmo:statement "Some people with diabetes have a blood pressure goal below 130/80 mm Hg.2,3 If you have heart disease or are at high risk for diabetes health problems, your goal may be lower. Ask your health care team what your goal should be." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Some people with diabetes have a blood pressure goal below 130/80 mm Hg.2,3 If you have heart disease or are at high risk for diabetes health problems, your goal may be lower. Ask your health care team what your goal should be." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/niddk-managing-diabetes> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/check-blood-glucose-level-at-home> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Check blood glucose level at home" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "check-blood-glucose-level-at-home" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Monitoring" ;
    dmo:statement "If you take insulin or other diabetes medicines, checking your blood glucose level at home may help you avoid high or low blood glucose levels. Even if you do not use insulin, checking your blood glucose level at home can help you manage your diabetes. The test results may help you and your health care team make changes to your meal plan, physical activity level, or diabetes medicines. It may help you understand how certain types of food affect your blood glucose level." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "If you take insulin or other diabetes medicines, checking your blood glucose level at home may help you avoid high or low blood glucose levels. Even if you do not use insulin, checking your blood glucose level at home can help you manage your diabetes. The test results may help you and your health care team make changes to your meal plan, physical activity level, or diabetes medicines. It may help you understand how certain types of food affect your blood glucose level." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/niddk-managing-diabetes> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/checking-urine-for-ketones> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Checking urine for ketones" ;
    dmo:populationScope "People with symptoms of diabetic ketoacidosis" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "checking-urine-for-ketones" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Screening" ;
    dmo:statement "Your health care team may want you to check your urine for ketones if you have symptoms of diabetic ketoacidosis." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Your health care team may want you to check your urine for ketones if you have symptoms of diabetic ketoacidosis." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/niddk-managing-diabetes> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/cholesterol-test> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Cholesterol test" ;
    dmo:gradingSystem "N/A" ;
    dmo:nativeEvidenceGrade "N/A" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Some people" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "cholesterol-test" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Monitoring" ;
    dmo:statement "Ask your health care team how often you need a cholesterol test NIH external link, also called a lipid panel, and what your cholesterol level should be. Some people may need to take a medicine called a statin External link, or another medicine, to lower their cholesterol for heart health." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Ask your health care team how often you need a cholesterol test NIH external link, also called a lipid panel, and what your cholesterol level should be. Some people may need to take a medicine called a statin External link, or another medicine, to lower their cholesterol for heart health." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/niddk-managing-diabetes> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/compare-cgm-readings-with-blood-glucose-meter> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Compare CGM readings with blood glucose meter" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "compare-cgm-readings-with-blood-glucose-meter" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Monitoring" ;
    dmo:statement "For safety, you may sometimes need to compare your CGM glucose readings with results from a standard blood glucose meter. This could be needed if you doubt the accuracy of your CGM readings, if you are changing your insulin dose, or if your CGM gives a warning alert." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "For safety, you may sometimes need to compare your CGM glucose readings with results from a standard blood glucose meter. This could be needed if you doubt the accuracy of your CGM readings, if you are changing your insulin dose, or if your CGM gives a warning alert." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/niddk-managing-diabetes> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/create-a-healthy-meal-plan> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Create a healthy meal plan" ;
    dmo:gradingSystem "N/A" ;
    dmo:nativeEvidenceGrade "N/A" ;
    dmo:populationScope "People with diabetes" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "create-a-healthy-meal-plan" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Lifestyle" ;
    dmo:statement "You may worry that having diabetes means going without foods you enjoy. The good news is that you can still eat your favorite foods, but you might need to eat smaller portions or enjoy them less often. Work with your health care team, which may include a registered dietitian or a diabetes educator, to create a meal plan that works for you." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "You may worry that having diabetes means going without foods you enjoy. The good news is that you can still eat your favorite foods, but you might need to eat smaller portions or enjoy them less often. Work with your health care team, which may include a registered dietitian or a diabetes educator, to create a meal plan that works for you." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/niddk-managing-diabetes> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/discuss-diabetes-self-care-plan-and-review-blood-glucose-chart-or-app> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Discuss diabetes self-care plan and review blood glucose chart or app" ;
    dmo:populationScope "People with diabetes" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "discuss-diabetes-self-care-plan-and-review-blood-glucose-chart-or-app" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Monitoring" ;
    dmo:statement "When you see your health care professional, discuss your diabetes self-care plan, review your blood glucose chart or app, and ask questions." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "When you see your health care professional, discuss your diabetes self-care plan, review your blood glucose chart or app, and ask questions." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/niddk-managing-diabetes> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/early-and-intensive-blood-glucose-management> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Early and intensive blood glucose management" ;
    dmo:gradingSystem "DCCT/EDIC study" ;
    dmo:nativeEvidenceGrade "High" ;
    dmo:populationScope "People with type 1 diabetes" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "early-and-intensive-blood-glucose-management" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Strong" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "Participants with type 1 diabetes who kept their blood glucose levels close to normal greatly lowered their chances of developing eye, kidney, and nerve disease." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "The study showed that participants with type 1 diabetes who kept their blood glucose levels close to normal greatly lowered their chances of developing eye, kidney, and nerve disease." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/niddk-managing-diabetes> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/early-and-intensive-blood-glucose-management-for-people-with-type-2-diabetes> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Early and intensive blood glucose management for people with type 2 diabetes" ;
    dmo:gradingSystem "Diabetes & Aging Study" ;
    dmo:nativeEvidenceGrade "High" ;
    dmo:populationScope "People with type 2 diabetes" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "early-and-intensive-blood-glucose-management-for-people-with-type-2-diabetes" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Strong" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "People with less effective diabetes management during the first year after being diagnosed with diabetes had a higher risk of diabetes complications and death." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "The study found that people with less effective diabetes management during the first year after being diagnosed with diabetes had a higher risk of diabetes complications and death." ;
