<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/get-enough-sleep> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Get enough sleep" ;
    dmo:gradingSystem "N/A" ;
    dmo:nativeEvidenceGrade "5" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Most adults" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "get-enough-sleep" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Lifestyle" ;
    dmo:statement "Getting enough sleep may improve your mood, energy level, and blood glucose level. Most adults should aim for about 7 to 8 hours each night.5 Children and adolescents may need more sleep." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Getting enough sleep may improve your mood, energy level, and blood glucose level. Most adults should aim for about 7 to 8 hours each night.5 Children and adolescents may need more sleep." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/niddk-managing-diabetes> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/get-physical-activity> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Get physical activity" ;
    dmo:gradingSystem "N/A" ;
    dmo:nativeEvidenceGrade "4" ;
    dmo:populationScope "People with diabetes" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "get-physical-activity" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Lifestyle" ;
    dmo:statement "Physical activity may help you lower blood glucose, blood pressure, and cholesterol levels. Being active may also help you get better sleep and improve your mood. Try to get at least 150 minutes of moderate-intensity External link physical activity, such as brisk walking, each week. If you can, try to do muscle-strengthening activities, such as wall push-ups or seated arm raises, two days a week.4" ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Physical activity may help you lower blood glucose, blood pressure, and cholesterol levels. Being active may also help you get better sleep and improve your mood. Try to get at least 150 minutes of moderate-intensity External link physical activity, such as brisk walking, each week. If you can, try to do muscle-strengthening activities, such as wall push-ups or seated arm raises, two days a week.4" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/niddk-managing-diabetes> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/keep-a-record-of-blood-glucose-self-checks> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Keep a record of blood glucose self-checks" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "keep-a-record-of-blood-glucose-self-checks" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Monitoring" ;
    dmo:statement "Make sure to keep a record of your blood glucose self-checks, including the date and time you checked it, the results, and other information, such as what you ate or what physical activity you did that day. You can use a chart or a smartphone app to help you keep track. Take this information with you when you visit your health care team." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Make sure to keep a record of your blood glucose self-checks, including the date and time you checked it, the results, and other information, such as what you ate or what physical activity you did that day. You can use a chart or a smartphone app to help you keep track. Take this information with you when you visit your health care team." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/niddk-managing-diabetes> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/keep-track-of-abcs-and-other-health-information> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Keep track of ABCs and other health information" ;
    dmo:populationScope "People with diabetes" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "keep-track-of-abcs-and-other-health-information" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Monitoring" ;
    dmo:statement "You may find it helpful to keep track of your ABCs and other important health information that you get during checkups with your primary care professional or other health care professionals." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "You may find it helpful to keep track of your ABCs and other important health information that you get during checkups with your primary care professional or other health care professionals." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/niddk-managing-diabetes> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/reach-and-maintain-a-healthy-weight> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Reach and maintain a healthy weight" ;
    dmo:gradingSystem "N/A" ;
    dmo:nativeEvidenceGrade "N/A" ;
    dmo:populationScope "People who are overweight or have obesity" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "reach-and-maintain-a-healthy-weight" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Lifestyle" ;
    dmo:statement "If you are overweight or have obesity, ask your health care team how you can manage your weight. To lose weight, you may need to consume fewer calories or get more physical activity. Your health care team may also recommend medicines or surgery to help manage your weight." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "If you are overweight or have obesity, ask your health care team how you can manage your weight. To lose weight, you may need to consume fewer calories or get more physical activity. Your health care team may also recommend medicines or surgery to help manage your weight." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/niddk-managing-diabetes> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/stop-smoking> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Stop smoking" ;
    dmo:gradingSystem "N/A" ;
    dmo:nativeEvidenceGrade "N/A" ;
    dmo:populationScope "People with diabetes" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "stop-smoking" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Lifestyle" ;
    dmo:statement "Not smoking is important for your health, especially if you have diabetes. Both smoking and diabetes can make your blood vessels narrow. E-cigarettes aren’t a safe option either. If you smoke, vape, or use other tobacco products, stop. Ask for help External link so you don’t have to do it alone." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Not smoking is important for your health, especially if you have diabetes. Both smoking and diabetes can make your blood vessels narrow. E-cigarettes aren’t a safe option either. If you smoke, vape, or use other tobacco products, stop. Ask for help External link so you don’t have to do it alone." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/niddk-managing-diabetes> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/take-care-of-your-mental-health> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Take care of your mental health" ;
    dmo:gradingSystem "N/A" ;
    dmo:nativeEvidenceGrade "N/A" ;
    dmo:populationScope "People with diabetes" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "take-care-of-your-mental-health" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Lifestyle" ;
    dmo:statement "Feeling stressed, sad, or angry can be common for people with diabetes. Many people with chronic, or long-term, illnesses such as diabetes develop anxiety or other mental health conditions NIH external link. Learn healthy ways to lower your stress NIH external link, and ask for help from your health care team or a mental health professional." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Feeling stressed, sad, or angry can be common for people with diabetes. Many people with chronic, or long-term, illnesses such as diabetes develop anxiety or other mental health conditions NIH external link. Learn healthy ways to lower your stress NIH external link, and ask for help from your health care team or a mental health professional." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/niddk-managing-diabetes> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/take-medicines-as-prescribed> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Take medicines as prescribed" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "take-medicines-as-prescribed" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "Take your medicines as they were prescribed, even if you feel good or have reached your blood glucose, blood pressure, or cholesterol goals. Avoid rationing your medicines or skipping taking your medicines if you have trouble paying for them. Talk with your health care team if you can’t afford your medicines or if you experience any side effects." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Take your medicines as they were prescribed, even if you feel good or have reached your blood glucose, blood pressure, or cholesterol goals. Avoid rationing your medicines or skipping taking your medicines if you have trouble paying for them. Talk with your health care team if you can’t afford your medicines or if you experience any side effects." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/niddk-managing-diabetes> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/talk-with-your-health-care-team-about-blood-glucose-targets> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Talk with your health care team about blood glucose targets" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "talk-with-your-health-care-team-about-blood-glucose-targets" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Monitoring" ;
    dmo:statement "Talk with your health care team about the blood glucose range that is healthy for you. Be sure to tell your health care team if your glucose levels frequently go above or below your target range." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Talk with your health care team about the blood glucose range that is healthy for you. Be sure to tell your health care team if your glucose levels frequently go above or below your target range." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/niddk-managing-diabetes> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/teach-family-friends-and-coworkers-how-to-use-glucagon> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Teach family, friends, and coworkers how to use glucagon" ;
    dmo:populationScope "People with a glucagon prescription" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "teach-family-friends-and-coworkers-how-to-use-glucagon" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Lifestyle" ;
    dmo:statement "If you have a glucagon prescription, you should teach your family, friends, and coworkers when and how to give you glucagon in case you are not able to do it yourself." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "If you have a glucagon prescription, you should teach your family, friends, and coworkers when and how to give you glucagon in case you are not able to do it yourself." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/niddk-managing-diabetes> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/track-time-in-range-for-cgm-users> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Track time in range for CGM users" ;
    dmo:populationScope "People who use a CGM" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "track-time-in-range-for-cgm-users" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Monitoring" ;
    dmo:statement "If you use a CGM, your health care team may ask you to keep track of your time in range. Time in range is the percentage of time that your glucose level stays in your target range. For many people with diabetes, the target range is between 70 and 180 mg/dL. Your health care team may adjust your diabetes care plan to help you stay in your target range at least 70% of the time." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "If you use a CGM, your health care team may ask you to keep track of your time in range. Time in range is the percentage of time that your glucose level stays in your target range. For many people with diabetes, the target range is between 70 and 180 mg/dL. Your health care team may adjust your diabetes care plan to help you stay in your target range at least 70% of the time." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/niddk-managing-diabetes> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/use-a-cgm-as-part-of-an-artificial-pancreas> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Use a CGM as part of an artificial pancreas" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "use-a-cgm-as-part-of-an-artificial-pancreas" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Treatment" ;
    dmo:statement "Some people use a CGM as part of an artificial pancreas. An artificial pancreas is a system that mimics how a healthy pancreas controls blood glucose in the body. A CGM, an insulin pump, and a software program that shares information between the CGM and insulin pump make up the artificial pancreas." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Some people use a CGM as part of an artificial pancreas. An artificial pancreas is a system that mimics how a healthy pancreas controls blood glucose in the body. A CGM, an insulin pump, and a software program that shares information between the CGM and insulin pump make up the artificial pancreas." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/niddk-managing-diabetes> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/use-a-continuous-glucose-monitor-cgm> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Use a continuous glucose monitor (CGM)" ;
    dmo:populationScope "People who take insulin to manage their diabetes" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "use-a-continuous-glucose-monitor-cgm" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Monitoring" ;
    dmo:statement "People who take insulin to manage their diabetes may benefit from using a continuous glucose monitor (CGM). A CGM uses a sensor in the tissue under your skin and shows changes in glucose levels throughout the day and night. Many CGM systems have alarms and warnings that let you know if your glucose level is too low or too high." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "People who take insulin to manage their diabetes may benefit from using a continuous glucose monitor (CGM). A CGM uses a sensor in the tissue under your skin and shows changes in glucose levels throughout the day and night. Many CGM systems have alarms and warnings that let you know if your glucose level is too low or too high." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/niddk-managing-diabetes> .

